---
code: K0020
title: Missing Closing Delimiter
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, delimiter, grouping]
description: "Opening delimiter is missing its matching closing delimiter"
---

An opening delimiter—such as `(`, `{`, `[`, or `<` in generic type parameters—was not matched with a corresponding closing delimiter (`)`, `}`, `]`, or `>`) before the end of the enclosing construct or file.

## Example

This error occurs when a block, argument list, sequence, record, or generic type argument list is left unclosed:

```kura
fn compute(x: Int, y: Int: Int => {
  let items = [1, 2, 3
  x + y
}
```

## Solution

Match every opening delimiter with its closing counterpart:

```kura
fn compute(x: Int, y: Int): Int => {
  let items = [1, 2, 3]
  x + y
}
```

If you are nesting generic types such as `Seq<Seq<Px>>`, note that the lexer tokenizes `>>` as two separate `>` tokens so both type argument lists close cleanly without needing a space between them.
